 "scope": "user network namespace on loopback, real binaries of v2.2.0, v2.3.0-rc3 and v2.3.0-rc4, every server with every client; the settings of the test node: USERS_FILE, OBFS_REQUIRE_MEMBER_KEY=true, REQUIRE_AUTH=true, member key on the client (PROXY_AUTH_MODE=member-only), UDP_NATIVE=true, UDP_PORT on the server, OBFS_MTU=1400, OBFS_MAX_PADDING=256",
 "checks": "per pair: 3 sequential and 8 parallel downloads of 4 MiB with sha256, 2 uploads of 4 MiB closed by SHUT_WR and answered with their sha256, 2 UDP associations of 320 datagrams of 200 bytes at 64 Hz to an echo; then SIGTERM to the client and to the server",
 "dial_checks": "with the client of v2.3.0-rc4 against each server, DIAL_TIMEOUT 10 s: 'refused' is the reply code and seconds of a CONNECT to a closed port; 'hole_open' and 'hole_closed' are 30 concurrent CONNECTs to an open and to a closed port behind an nftables rule that drops a third of the flows by a hash of the source address and port, counted by reply code and by the time of the reply, in bins that end 0.3 s after each backup of rc4 (0.5, 1.5, 3, 5 and 7 s), the last one holding the replies at the end of the budget; the open port accepts and closes at once; 'blackhole' is a CONNECT to an address that drops every packet: sockets of the server in SYN-SENT at 2 s and 8 s, the reply, and the sockets left after it. Reply codes: 0 success, 1 general failure, 4 host unreachable (the budget ran out), 5 connection refused. Every reply 1 here is the client failing to read a success reply that arrived together with the end of the stream (client_connect_reply_eof, draft finding Ч-22), not a failure of the dial",
 "build": "CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build -trimpath -buildvcs=false -ldflags \"-s -w -X github.com/mazixs/S5Core/internal/buildinfo.version=<tag>\" ./cmd/<binary>, go 1.26.6, from the tags v2.2.0 and v2.3.0-rc3 and from the tree of v2.3.0-rc4; the same command gives the same bytes, and the server of v2.3.0-rc4 is the /S5Core of the published image",
